# Refactor context lives in git

When you amend refactor project context, land it on the **active branch** in the same change set as the work that motivated it. Do not leave updates only in the Cursor Project agent store.

Commit together with related work (or a dedicated docs commit on that branch):

| Artifact | Repo path |
| --- | --- |
| Migration plan, project context, parity target | `docs/refactor/` |
| Feature map | `.cursor/rules/feature-map.mdc` |
| Endpoint map | `.cursor/maps/endpoint-map.yaml` |
| Agent skills | `.cursor/skills/` |

Implementation slices stay **paused** until Tobias says resume. Store-only scratch (`notes.md`, `internal/` harvests, worker transcripts) does not belong in the repo.
